[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
Podman Desktop talks to the rootful podman API socket
/var/run/podman/podman.sock. Enable and start the podman service:

  # sysrc podman_service_enable=YES
  # service podman_service start

The socket is only accessible to root by default. To use Podman Desktop as a
regular user, give your user access to /var/run/podman/podman.sock, for
example with a dedicated group, after the service has started:

  # pw groupadd podman
  # pw groupmod podman -m <user>
  # chgrp podman /var/run/podman/podman.sock
  # chmod 660 /var/run/podman/podman.sock

Containers on FreeBSD are jails managed by sysutils/ocijail, see
https://podman.io/docs/installation#installing-on-freebsd-140 for the
required pf(4)/ZFS setup. Podman machine (VM) features are not available.
EOM
}
]
